# Language — public English / private Japanese

**Rule Rev.3** — 2026-09-13 (common)

**Precedence:** DialKey `.cursor/rules` is the latest. The older essay
`project_standards/app_spec_rules.md` does not override it. Copy common
files DialKey → this kit → other projects. A product overlay in the same
file is for that project. Current product behaviour follows the public spec.

| Surface | Language |
|---|---|
| Code, identifiers, comments | English |
| Public spec, README, docs site, in-app Help, CLI `--help` | **English** |
| Committed `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (this kit) | **English** |
| Author-only notes (`private_spec.md`, other `private_*`) | **Japanese OK** |
| Chat / design discussion | Japanese OK |
| UI strings | English built-in; optional `lang/<code>.toml` overlays |
| User data (slot names, paths) | Any language; do not translate |

Do not write the public spec in Japanese. Do not copy Japanese author notes into Help, the docs site, or the public spec.

When a public paragraph sounds like a memoir, tax note, or discarded-idea diary, move it to `private_*` and leave an English fact (or delete it).
